From 0ecbb5e0b4eb4fffbb8093b3394da403e892e632 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 11:49:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0276 -- #6 UX: "Press ESC to skip" note on the organya
 precache overlay

Operator-requested after 0275 let the organya cold-cache precache actually run
(~19 min / 47 MB one-time on the POD-83). The ESC-skip already works (during the
first-launch batch, ESC sets g_oc_abort -> aborts the precache -> songs
cold-render on demand in-game, no data loss); this just tells the user it's
there. Adds one dim-gray centered line "Press ESC to skip (songs render during
play)" below the progress bars in _oc_draw_progress. GATED batch-only
(g_oc_batch_active): in an in-game cold-render ESC is the gameplay pause key (the
beat cb never aborts there), so the hint must not show then or it would be a lie.
Cosmetic; no behavior change. Batches with setup-eng's SETUP one-time-cost
description into one follow-up build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/main.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index dc9d0b50..c90b92fd 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -1445,6 +1445,17 @@ static void _oc_draw_progress(uint32_t cur_beat, uint32_t total_beats)
       r->fillRect(bx0 + 1, iy + 1, bx0 + 1 + fillw, iy + 5, 0x40, 0xC0, 0xFF);
   }
 
+  // patch 0276 (#6 UX): ESC-skip hint. ONLY in the first-launch batch, where ESC
+  // sets g_oc_abort -> aborts the precache -> songs cold-render on demand in-game
+  // (no data loss). In an in-game cold-render (overlay B) ESC is the gameplay
+  // pause key -- the beat cb returns 0 there and never aborts -- so the hint must
+  // NOT show then or it would be a lie. Dim gray, centered, below the bars.
+  if (g_oc_batch_active)
+  {
+    const char *skip = "Press ESC to skip (songs render during play)";
+    r->font.draw((W - (int)r->font.getWidth(skip)) / 2, H / 2 + 30, skip, 0x909090, true);
+  }
+
   _oc_step("before flip");
   r->flip();
   _oc_step("after flip");
-- 
